Chapter: CityWorkers
  cites Uoaix chapter CompositeGatherer
  cites Uoaix chapter Cities

 A city's ore box is the 8 x 8 blocks densest in rock faces its entrance walks to (a standable tile beside MiningTiles land,
 on the 1.25 statics; Minoc's hills at a climb of 4): boxes on the mountain itself held no clear tile and founded no miner
 or quarrier in Minoc, Cove or Buccaneer's Den (live 43347).
  cw-none : BbShop = BbShop { title = "None", premises = "None", x1 = 1, y1 = 1, x2 = 0, y2 = 0 }
  cw-held : BbShop -> Boolean
  cw-held (r) = r.x1 <= r.x2 & r.y1 <= r.y2
  cw-vendor-for : List CtCity, List BbShop, List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  cw-vendor-for (cities) (shops) (roles) (city) (role) (k) = if k >= list-length shops | k >= list-length roles then -1
    else let s = list-at shops k
    in if list-at roles k == role & ct-city-at cities s.x1 s.y1 0 == city then bb-shop-count + k
    else cw-vendor-for cities shops roles city role (k + 1)
  cw-vendors : List CtCity, List BbShop, List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  cw-vendors (cities) (shops) (roles) (city) (n) (role) (out) = if role >= n then out
    else cw-vendors cities shops roles city n (role + 1) (out & [cw-vendor-for cities shops roles city role 0])
  cw-house : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> CggHouse
  cw-house (dx) (dy) (x1) (y1) (x2) (y2) = CggHouse { door = BbSpot { x = dx, y = dy, z = 0 }, floor = BbShop { title = "Home", premises = "House", x1 = x1, y1 = y1, x2 = x2, y2 = y2 } }
  cw-box : Text, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> BbShop
  cw-box (title) (x1) (y1) (x2) (y2) = BbShop { title = title, premises = "Skara Brae", x1 = x1, y1 = y1, x2 = x2, y2 = y2 }
 Skara Brae (city 5). Houses: the rooms behind its unsigned doors (UOX3 felucca_doors.jsdata, no felucca_signs.jsdata
 sign within 4 tiles), floors bounded by the 1.25 statics' walls. Woods and gardens: the 8 x 8 blocks of its window
 holding the most trees (art 0x0CCA-0x0CEA, 0x0D94-0x0DA8, 0x12B6-0x12C7) and wild plants (0x0C80-0x0C8F,
 0x0CA0-0x0CBF, 0x0D00-0x0D4F) in the 1.25 STATICS0. The island holds no mountain land, field or pasture. The inn door
 is The Falconer's Inn's (UOX3 doors 615,2234 and 615,2235); the stations are the counters of On Guard Armory, Shear
 Pleasure and Builders' Delight.
