 Minoc (city 13; reek's W2 survey). Its ground-floor houses (the upper rooms at z 15 stand off cw-house's door height),
 the first of them its lodging (no innkeeper keeps a Minoc inn); its ore is the mountain strip east of town, its shore the
 river row; no field, pasture, herbalist or woods (UOAIX-234), so it founds a fisherman, miners and a quarrier as its keepers buy.
